  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-260000017</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Leading from the South pooled fund to strengthen local Women&apos;s Rights Organisations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity is supporting the Leading from the South consortium and builds on MFA support to LFS from its inception in 2016 until 2025. The consortium consists of four regional women&apos;s funds from the global South and has been successful for almost ten years in supporting women&apos;s rights organizations and women&apos;s movements in the global South. The activity has 3 strategies to achieve gender equality and promote women&apos;s rights in a highly localized way:
1. provide flexible grants and capacity-building to women&apos;s rights organizations in a demand-driven, bottom-up way (78% of total).
2. linking and learning between organizations, themes and regions to jointly strategize around common goals and learn from each other.
3. setting up a pooled fund in order to create a stronger funding landscape for Southern women&apos;s rights organizations.
This activity is with Women&apos;s Fund Asia as the lead organization for the LFS consortium.</narrative>
  </description>
